# The family's baseline block, byte-identical in every checkout that carries it,
# so what a routine editable install or test run drops is ignored in the repo
# that drops it. The eleven files were written independently and covered
# different subsets of the same artifacts, which left several trees dirty after
# a plain `pip install -e .` -- and a dirty tree here blocks every agent's merge.
# This repo's own entries go under the marker below, never in here.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tmp-pytest-*/

# Windows shortcuts are machine-specific and embed the real install path.
*.lnk

# pCloud conflict copies (this dir syncs via pCloud). Never our files; an
# untracked one dirties main and blocks merges. '[' escaped to match literally.
*\[conflicted*

# --- fun_time's own ---

# Where the app works: what it has put away, and what it is doing now.
archive/
state/
favs.csv

# Named in this repo's pytest config as a directory not to walk into.
pytest-cache-files-*/

# The baseline's *.egg-info/ is not just cruft here: the integration runner
# stamps a run's row `-dirty` when `git status` is not empty, so an artifact
# every installed checkout carries would mark every run and the flag would stop
# meaning anything.

# Private overlays — real values live here and never get published. Each has a
# committed *.example.* template that documents its shape.
#   real runtime config (paths to the library, provider URLs): use the example
/fun_time_config.json
#   real copy — filter vocabulary and other content: use content.example.json
/content.local.json
#   real userscript — provider-specific autofill: use regen_autofill.example.user.js
/fun_time/static/regen_autofill.user.js

# Visual Studio / IDE cruft
.vs/

# Internal dev logs — explicit project history, kept local, not published
/docs/refactor-log.md
/playnav_HUDs_logs_toasts.md
